arm64: fix the os-prober record emitted for EFI bootloaders

The factor-out-logger patch redirects result() to fd_result, which os-prober
exports as 3 and maps onto real stdout. 05efi captures its EFI subtests with
command substitution, so the subtest record escaped straight into os-prober's
output and $entry stayed empty: os-prober emitted the bare
"<path>:<long>:<label>" record instead of
"<partition>@/<efi dir>/<path>:<long>:<label>:efi", which grub2-mkconfig
cannot use ("cannot find a GRUB drive for ...",
"... is not yet supported by grub-mkconfig").

os-prober-factored-logger-efi-fix.patch does this for the x86 copy of 05efi
only; do the same for the arm64 copy.

diff --git a/os-probes/mounted/arm64/05efi b/os-probes/mounted/arm64/05efi
index fcf3697..493a23e 100755
--- a/os-probes/mounted/arm64/05efi
+++ b/os-probes/mounted/arm64/05efi
@@ -59,7 +59,11 @@ ret=1
 for test in /usr/lib/os-probes/mounted/efi/*; do
 	debug "running subtest $test"
 	if [ -f "$test" ] && [ -x "$test" ]; then
+		# we need results of subtest in stdout
+		orig_fd_res=$fd_result
+		export fd_result=1
 		entry=$("$test" "$mpoint/$efi")
+		export fd_result=$orig_fd_res
 		if [ -n "$entry" ]; then
 			debug "bootloader $entry found by subtest $test"
 			ret=0
